    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1982-p2.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Eight times \\(x,\\) increased by two, is \\(8x+2.\\) One fourth is \\(\\frac{8x+2}{4}=2x+\\frac12.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "Translate the first two operations before dividing",
        "Simplify \\(\\frac{8x+2}{4}\\) term by term"
      ],
